        "## What the bill provides",
        "- **Presumption of employment.** A person working through a platform, including a passenger transport driver, does not have to prove they are an employee. It is the platform that must show there is no employment relationship.\n- **Existing contracts.** The presumption will also cover contracts in force on the day the act takes effect, for periods from 2 December 2026.\n- **Joint and several liability.** The platform is jointly and severally liable with the intermediary that settles the worker's pay. In passenger transport, this intermediary is usually the fleet partner – a company that handles licences, settlements and often vehicles for app drivers, a typical feature of the Polish market ([see our guide](/en/guide/polish-taxi-market-explained)).\n- **Algorithmic management.** Automated decisions, such as blocking an account, are to be subject to human oversight.",
